.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH mnnn-journal-export 1  "mnnn-journal-export 2.1.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-journal\-export \- Export a journal (or some entries) as PDF, Word, HTML, LaTeX, text or JSON (JSON can be imported again)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn journal export\fR [\fB\-\-entry\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIJOURNAL\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Export a journal (or some entries) as PDF, Word, HTML, LaTeX, text or JSON (JSON can be imported again)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-entry\fR \fI<ENTRIES>\fR
Only these entries. Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: pdf]

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
pdf
.IP \(bu 2
html
.IP \(bu 2
docx
.IP \(bu 2
latex
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
csv
.IP \(bu 2
text
.IP \(bu 2
archive
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Output file (default: <name>.<ext> in the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIJOURNAL\fR>

.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.1.0
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
